The {{Term/Store|Royal Guard Cap|Royal Guard Caps|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Allies"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Royal Guard Cap is obtained through the "[[EX Royal Guard Rumors]]" [[Side Quest]], which is exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack. During the Side Quest, [[Link]] is required to read the ''[[Super Rumor Mill V4]]'', which is located at [[Riverside Stable]].<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> Within, [[Traysi]] claims that pieces of the [[Royal Guard Set]] can be found in the [[Dining Hall]], near the [[Guards' Chamber]], and on the second floor.<ref name="BotW Super Rumor Mill V4"/>

The Royal Guard Cap can be found in a [[Hidden Chest]] in [[Champions' Hall]], which is located on the second floor of the [[Sanctum]] of [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]]. After it has been found, [[Granté]] will begin to sell it in [[Tarrey Town]].{{Note|Prior to the [[The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild#Updates|Version 1.3.3 Update]], Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the ''[[Breath of the Wild Expansion Pass]]''. This meant that the Royal Guard Cap could not be replaced if sold.}} The Cap is part of the Royal Guard Set, along with the [[Royal Guard Boots]] and [[Royal Guard Uniform]].<ref name="CaC 190"/> Wearing all three pieces of [[Armor]] will decrease the amount of [[Stamina]] Link uses during a charge attack. The Royal Guard Cap cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]] or [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

